===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|Milky Way Galaxy}} {{l|en|Galaxy}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|galaxye}}, {{m|enm|galaxie}}, from {{der|en|fro|galaxie}}, from {{der|en|la|galaxias}}, from {{der|en|grc|γαλαξίας||Milky Way}}, shortening of {{m|grc|γαλαξίας κύκλος||milky circle}}, from {{m|grc|γάλα||milk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡæl.ək.si/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-galaxy.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|rare}} The [[Milky Way]]; the apparent band of concentrated stars which appears in the night sky over earth. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1633|author=w:John Donne|title=Sapho to Philænis|passage=So may thy cheekes red outweare scarlet dye, / And their white, whitenesse of the '''''Galaxie''''' [...].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1833|author=Thomas Keightley|authorlink=Thomas Keightley|title=Fairy Mythology|publisher=William Harrison Ainsworth|location=London|volume=I|page=5|text=Grecian imagination ascribed to the '''galaxy''' or milky way an origin in the teeming breast of the queen of heaven[.]}}
# {{senseid|en|Q318}}{{lb|en|galaxy}} Any of the collections of many millions or billions of stars, [[galactic]] dust, [[black hole]]s, etc. existing as independent and coherent [[system]]s, of which there are billions in the known [[universe]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[assemblage]] of things or people seen as [[luminous]] or [[brilliant]].
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=Dec 1936|journal=Thrilling Wonder Stories|page=127|column=1|passage=[a] '''galaxy''' of science fiction stars.}}
# {{rfd-sense|en|section=galaxy,_sense_#4}} {{lb|en|fashion|design}} Any [[print]] or [[pattern]] reminiscent of a galaxy, generally consisting of [[blending]], [[semiopaque]] patches of vibrant color on a dark background.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Reyna Young|title=Hanover Falls|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=3TKoDAAAQBAJ&pg=PA42&dq=%22galaxy+wallpaper%22|page=42|passage=Her walls and ceiling were covered with '''galaxy''' wallpaper; it was like stepping into space.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Rebekah L. Purdy|title=Incriminating Dating|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=dGtqDgAAQBAJ&pg=PT178&dq=%22galaxy+leggings%22|passage=Her nerdy glasses sat perched on her face, and she wore a May the Force Be With You T-shirt with a black lace skirt, '''galaxy''' leggings, and a pair of white Star Wars Vans.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Isabel Scheck|title=Survival|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=6jRwDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA15&dq=%22galaxy+blanket%22|page=15|passage=She hurriedly said that she found an{{sic}} faded '''galaxy''' blanket. She loved '''galaxy''' patterned things.}}

